<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><office:document xmlns:office="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:office:1.0" xmlns:text="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:text:1.0" xmlns:table="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:table:1.0" office:version="1.3" office:mimetype="application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.text"><office:body><office:text><text:p># CORRECTED DRAFT — REVIEW REQUIRED</text:p><text:p>SELF-CREATED FICTIONAL PRACTICE EVENT</text:p><text:p></text:p><text:p>Riverside Reading Day is planned for Saturday, 17 October 2026, at Cedar Hall. The public programme runs from 10:00 to 14:00. Admission is free, and maximum public attendance is 120 people.</text:p><text:p></text:p><text:p>The event is intended for readers aged 8 and above. Children must attend with a responsible adult. Cedar Hall has level access at the main entrance and an accessible toilet. A quiet room is not available.</text:p><text:p></text:p><text:p>The current planned cost is 575 credits, calculated from the four listed budget items. Credits are fictional teaching units.</text:p><text:p></text:p><text:p>**DO NOT PUBLISH UNTIL OPEN QUESTIONS ARE RESOLVED.**</text:p><text:p></text:p><text:p>## Open questions</text:p><text:p>1. What parking is available, and what does it cost?</text:p><text:p>2. Who receives volunteer registrations?</text:p><text:p>3. What is the volunteer registration deadline?</text:p><text:p></text:p><text:p>Owner: fictional event organizer — answers not supplied.</text:p><text:p></text:p><text:p>## Source notes — opened and checked during the worked review</text:p><text:p>01_Event_Brief.md — Overview, Audience, Volunteer registration.</text:p><text:p>02_Schedule.md — Public Programme.</text:p><text:p>03_Venue_Note.md — Capacity and Access, Parking.</text:p><text:p>04_Budget.csv — spreadsheet rows 2–5 (header is row 1).</text:p></office:text></office:body></office:document>
